205	1432,565,1645,982	205 Nut and Cupule.	An acorn on a short stalk: the smooth, egg-shaped nut sitting in its scaly cup.
206	86,1212,192,1774	Fig. 206.	The key of the Ash: a long, narrow, strap-like wing, finely lined, with the seed in its lower end and a slender stalk below.
207	53,1822,228,2100	207 Key.	The key of the Elm: a round, flat, net-veined wing with the seed in its middle and a notch at the top.
208	285,1667,630,2096	208 Pair of Keys.	The fruit of the Maple: two keys joined at the base on one stalk, each a seed with a long veined wing spreading upwards.
209	1393,1668,1647,2093	209 Opened Follicle.	The simple pod of a Marsh-Marigold opened out flat after ripening, like a veined leaf, with small scars along its edges where the seeds were borne.
